From a94fcb1452a28946af26c084fb99199ff8dac23c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(trace): report the FingerprintException where TLC's
 own value methods fail, and not where Tool does

Two places where the failure replay reported a FingerprintException
where TLC reports the nested expressions, or the reverse:

- A state check that fails as the initial predicate's last conjunct
  enumerates a set (Init == x \in 0..1 /\ y \in {0}, Inv == 1). TLC
  checks the state from Tool.getInitStates, after the set's enumerator
  returned, so the failure is in no method of the set; the replay took
  the walked conjunct's set as the failing receiver. A failure from what
  a walk goes on to no longer marks the frame it passes.
- A set of functions over Nat, which TLC enumerates by its own method
  (SetOfFcnsValue.elements) as the set of a quantifier or a set map, and
  as the base of a set filter TLC keeps lazy. Its source heads the
  FingerprintException; Cardinality, a Java method, reports that as its
  own failure (2154).

29 runs of the upstream conformance suite now print what TLC prints;
fingerprint-exceptions.txt records the shapes from the pinned jar.
